# Cursor Rule: Risk Network Visualization System - Simple & Flexible Structure

## Project Overview
This rule defines a simple, scalable folder structure for the Risk Network Visualization System that can grow organically as features are added.

## Core Folder Structure

```
src/cro_rmi_improvement_feature/network_analyzer/
├── app/                          # Main Dash application
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py                   # Dash app entry point
│   ├── layout.py                 # Main app layout
│   ├── callbacks.py              # Dash callbacks (can split later)
│   └── assets/                   # Static assets
│       ├── styles.css
│       └── custom.js
├── core/                         # Core business logic
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── models.py                 # Data models (can split later)
│   ├── services.py               # Business logic (can split later)
│   └── utils.py                  # Utility functions
├── data/                         # Raw data storage
│   ├── raw/                      # Raw Excel files and input data
│   └── processed/                # Processed data files
├── data_processor/               # Data processing and management
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── processing.py             # Data processing (can split later)
│   └── storage.py                # Data storage
├── ai/                           # AI components (Phase 2)
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── classifier.py             # Risk relationship classification
│   └── cache.py                  # AI response caching
├── visualization/                # Visualization components
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── layouts.py                # Graph layout algorithms
│   └── styling.py                # Graph styling
├── tests/                        # Tests (can expand later)
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── test_basic.py
├── config/                       # Configuration
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── settings.py
├── tasks/                        # Task management (existing)
│   ├── tasks.json
│   └── PRD.md
├── .cursor/                      # Cursor rules (existing)
│   └── rules/
├── requirements.txt              # Dependencies
├── README.md                     # Project documentation
└── main.py                       # Application entry point
```

## Growth Principles

### 1. Start Simple, Split When Needed
**✅ DO:**
- Start with single files for each major component
- Split files when they exceed 300-500 lines
- Create subdirectories when you have 3+ related files

**Example Growth Pattern:**
```
# Phase 1: Single files
app/callbacks.py (200 lines) ✅ Keep as is

# Phase 2: Growing complexity
app/callbacks.py (600 lines) ❌ Split into:
app/callbacks/
├── __init__.py
├── graph_callbacks.py
├── filter_callbacks.py
└── company_callbacks.py
```

### 2. Feature-Based Organization
**✅ DO:**
- Group related functionality together
- Create new top-level folders for major features
- Keep related files close to each other

**Example:**
```
# When adding API features
api/
├── __init__.py
├── routes.py
└── middleware.py

# When adding deployment
deployment/
├── Dockerfile
└── docker-compose.yml
```

### 3. Naming Conventions
**✅ DO:**
- Use snake_case for files and folders
- Use descriptive names that indicate purpose
- Keep names short but clear

**Examples:**
```
✅ Good:
- risk_models.py
- graph_service.py
- data_processing.py

❌ Bad:
- models.py
- service.py
- processing.py
```

### 4. Import Organization
**✅ DO:**
- Use relative imports within the project
- Group imports: standard library, third-party, local
- Keep imports at the top of files

**Example:**
```python
# Standard library imports
import json
import os
from typing import Dict, List

# Third-party imports
import dash
import pandas as pd

# Local imports
from ..core.models import RiskNode
from ..data.processing import load_data
```

